codex
The gitignore route has a concrete uncovered adopter case: `.claude/.gitignore` is preserved wholesale whenever it already exists, even if it lacks both required entries. That leaves user-ceremony installs/upgrades unprotected because those routes intentionally never touch the root `.gitignore`; all new efficacy scenarios start from an empty target, so their controls cannot expose this case. I’m now checking the npm vocabulary sweep and workflow claims for the same “green but incomplete scope” pattern.
