   186	# rather than leave the reader to find out: the SIDECAR verifies (it names one
   187	# file, and that file was just built). The cumulative manifest does NOT verify
   188	# as a whole — it keeps lines for tarballs of OTHER versions, `npm/*.tgz` is
   189	# git-ignored so a fresh clone has none of them on disk, and a bulk check
   190	# therefore exits non-zero on "No such file or directory" for every line but
   191	# the current one. Measured, not assumed (PLAN-177 W1). Compare the single
