1. **P1 — `.claude/.gitignore` delivery is incomplete.**  
   **FILE:LINE:** [scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:858](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:858)  
   **Failure scenario:** If an adopter already has `.claude/.gitignore` without `/state/` and `/settings.local.json`, the helper returns without adding them. Under `--ceremony user`, the root `.gitignore` is deliberately untouched, so `/night-mode on` still leaves both artifacts visible to Git—the exact P1-1 defect. All efficacy scenarios start with no `.claude/.gitignore`, so their positive controls cannot catch this.  
   **Minimal fix:** Preserve existing content but append each missing anchored rule idempotently. Add user install and upgrade tests seeded with an unrelated pre-existing `.claude/.gitignore`.

2. **P1 — The npm honesty sweep leaves published Level-3 claims intact.**  
   **FILE:LINE:** [npm/README.md:87](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/npm/README.md:87), [README.pt-BR.md:96](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/README.pt-BR.md:96), [INSTALL.md:19](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/INSTALL.md:19), [docs/QUICKSTART.md:86](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/docs/QUICKSTART.md:86)  
   **Failure scenario:** npm consumers receive `npm/README.md`, which still promises “SLSA 3 provenance”; the quickstarts repeat Level 3, and INSTALL/Portuguese README also promise broader checksum coverage. The workflow and corrected English README provide Level 2 and an `install.sh`-only checksum. The new semantic test inspects only root `README.md`, so it passes while the package’s own README remains false.  
   **Minimal fix:** Correct every live and shipped consumer document, including translations, and run the SLSA/checksum vocabulary gate over an explicit exhaustive surface list rather than only root README.

3. **P1 — The replacement npm verification recipe does not verify the advertised global install.**  
   **FILE:LINE:** [SUPPORT.md:155](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/SUPPORT.md:155), [npm/INTEGRITY.md:99](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/npm/INTEGRITY.md:99)  
   **Failure scenario:** The supported channel is `npm install -g`, followed by advice to use `npm audit signatures`. npm does not support signature audits of global packages; without `--global`, it audits the current project instead, and the extra `ceo-orchestration` positional argument does not select that package. A user can therefore obtain either an error or a successful audit that never examined the installed shim.  
   **Minimal fix:** Point global/npx users to the npm provenance panel, or provide a local project installation recipe followed by `npm audit signatures`. Add a regression assertion that the documented command’s install scope matches what npm audits.

4. **P1 — The candidate’s canonical limitation text says the cured decision defect is still open.**  
   **FILE:LINE:** [CLAUDE.md:94](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/CLAUDE.md:94)  
   **Failure scenario:** It states that the validator contains zero `GO`/`NO-GO` occurrences and that a negative verdict still authorizes release. At this SHA, the validator rejects `NO-GO` with exit 3 and the fail-closed tag guard also checks the decision. Operators and future model sessions are therefore given the opposite of the implemented release contract.  
   **Minimal fix:** Remove the obsolete open-P1 paragraph or replace it with an accurate statement of the two decision gates and their accepted set.

5. **P1 — The S303 harness filter creates a false-green class.**  
   **FILE:LINE:** [.claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:537](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/.claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:537), [.claude/scripts/tests/test_ceo_boot.py:668](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc4.V1tu8w/wt/.claude/scripts/tests/test_ceo_boot.py:668)  
   **Failure scenario:** The predicate never checks the known probe description/hash. Any markerless real spawn—including one admitted because the PreToolUse hook failed open—is classified as a harness probe and removed from the denominator. A direct probe using an unrelated description and hash returned green with `harness_probes_skipped=1`. The negative control adds one governed marker, so it never tests the dangerous all-absent/non-probe shape.  
   **Minimal fix:** Require a closed, observed harness signature, preferably the exact description hash plus the structural fields. Add a negative control with all five fields absent but a different description/hash and require the ratio to turn red.

The decision gate and tournament workdir cure themselves behaved correctly in focused probes, but these remaining P1s make the payload incomplete and introduce false assurance.

